WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.380
Centralized processing sends multiple feeds to one local server or cluster.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:11.320
It simplifies model management, dashboards, storage integration, and capacity pooling.

3
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:19.020
It also creates a shared bandwidth path and a larger failure domain, so redundancy and overload behavior need attention.

4
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.300
Edge processing runs some analysis near each camera or site.

5
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:29.320
This can reduce upstream bandwidth and keep decisions available during connectivity loss.

6
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:36.860
Edge devices have limited compute and create a distributed fleet that must be secured, updated, observed, and supported.

7
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:45.620
A hybrid architecture performs lightweight filtering locally and sends selected events to a central or approved cloud service for deeper analysis.

8
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:53.960
This can balance privacy, latency, and model capability, but every external data transfer must be explicit and governed.

9
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.760
NVR-integrated analysis uses the recording platform as the stream and event hub.

10
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:05.940
It may be easier to operate, though model flexibility and hardware choices can be constrained by the vendor.

11
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:13.960
Batch review analyzes stored clips later, while near-real-time processing favors timely alerts at higher continuous compute cost.

12
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.160
No pattern wins every tradeoff.

13
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.380
Centralization favors simplicity and shared resources.

14
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.960
Edge favors locality and resilience.

15
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.420
Hybrid designs can scale selectively but add integration and data-flow complexity.

16
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:37.460
Choose by use case, camera count, network capacity, event urgency, privacy, cost, model size, support skills, and acceptable failure modes.

17
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:45.880
A fleet can use different patterns for different cameras, provided policy, identity, time, and review remain consistent.
